    <!-- Darts screen strings. Prefixed dt_. -->
    <string name="dt_help_title">How to play Darts</string>
    <string name="dt_help_text">Drag on the board to move the reticle, then flick upward to throw. A moderate flick is best: a soft one sags low and a hard one wobbles. The Throw button and the arrow and target buttons do the same without a swipe. In 501 and 301 count down to exactly zero, finishing on a double unless double out is off; going past zero is a bust and the visit does not count. In Cricket close 20, 19, 18, 17, 16, 15 and the bull with three marks each, then score on numbers your rivals have not closed. After three darts, collect them to pass the turn.</string>
